    <p>The point is not that a Builder must code. Building shows up in fabrication, design, engineering, and skilled trades too. Welding, for example, is projected to grow only 2%, yet the trade turns over about 45,600 openings a year, so hands-on making stays in demand even where headline growth is flat (<a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/production/welders-cutters-solderers-and-brazers.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS, 2025</a>). Best Answer Hub tags each match with an AI outlook so you can see where making is amplified by AI and where it stays firmly human-led.</p>

    <div class="cav">The honest bit</div>
    <h2 id="ai">Does AI threaten people whose strength is building?</h2>
    <p>AI changes what building looks like, but it raises the value of build judgment rather than removing it. Best Answer Hub tags every matched maker role with an honest AI outlook rather than a reassuring one. The picture from the field is split: a controlled GitHub trial found developers finished a coding task 55% faster with an AI assistant, so the rote scaffolding really is getting automated (<a href="https://github.blog/news-insights/research/research-quantifying-github-copilots-impact-on-developer-productivity-and-happiness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub, 2022</a>). At the same time, in Stack Overflow's 2025 survey of about 49,000 developers, 84% use or plan to use AI tools, but only 33% trust their accuracy, 66% are most frustrated by answers that are almost right but not quite, and 45% say debugging AI code takes longer than expected (<a href="https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2025/ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stack Overflow, 2025</a>).</p>
    <figure class="chart">
      <figcaption class="chart-title">Developers use AI, but do not trust it to finish the job</figcaption>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 600 285" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart: 84 percent of developers use AI tools, 33 percent trust its accuracy, 45 percent say debugging AI code takes longer than expected">
        <defs><linearGradient id="aigrad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#C6603F"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#8a4429"/></linearGradient></defs>
