      <li>NIST, <a href="https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/2021/03/24/econImpactSumm.v23.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Economic Impacts of Inadequate Software Testing</a>, 2002 ($59.5B a year; over half of errors found late).</li>
      <li>World Economic Forum, <a href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/in-full/3-skills-outlook/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Future of Jobs Report 2025, Skills Outlook</a> (analytical and creative thinking among fastest-rising skills).</li>
      <li>Schmidt, F. and Hunter, J., <a href="https://psycnet.apa.org/record/1998-10661-006" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Validity and Utility of Selection Methods</a>, Psychological Bulletin, 1998 (work samples among the strongest predictors).</li>
      <li>LinkedIn, <a href="https://linkedin.github.io/skills-first-report/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Skills-First Report</a>, 2024 (88% of hirers say degree screens filter out skilled people).</li>
      <li>Harvard Business School, <a href="https://www.hbs.edu/managing-the-future-of-work/research/Pages/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Managing the Future of Work</a>, 2024 (skills-based hiring slower in practice than in policy).</li>
    </ul>
